You could say {.i ca'e .a'y by cy cibjgatai gi'e se jipno .a'y .e by .e=20
cy} for "Let ABC be a triangle with A, B and C as its vertexes."
You then can refer back to it with {.a'y by cy} ("ABC") as a pronoun.y

For talking about the length of a segment [AB], you can just say {lo ni=20
.a'y darno by ku} or {lo se darlai be .a'y bei by (ku)}, "the distance=20
between A and B".

